 - **Fail-fast XML lookup hardening:** replaced almost all `getInfoTypeForString(...)` calls (terrain/features/bonuses and similar tags) with `getInfoTypeOrFail(...)` (in [SASUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SASUtils.py)), so **missing/renamed XML tags raise explicit errors** instead of silently using invalid `-1` values. Notably allowed to detect and fix incorrect `getInfoTypeOrFail("DIRECTION_NORTH")` instead of correct `DirectionTypes.DIRECTION_NORTH` (in Planet Generator map), or incorrect `getInfoTypeOrFail("PLOT_PEAK")` failing instead of correct `PlotTypes.PLOT_PEAK` (in Peirce map).
 - **Static define-key audit:** added [`audit_define_keys.py`](/LLM_Helpers/audit_define_keys.py), which statically greps every literal `getDefine{BOOL,FLOAT,INT,STRING}("X")` call across Python and DLL and verifies `X` is declared in mod XML, base BTS XML, or vanilla Civ4 XML. Catches **per-key drift** (renamed/removed XML entries) before runtime. A runtime fail-loud wrapper isn't practical here because `getDefine*` returns `0`/`""` for both missing and legitimately zero/empty keys (unlike `getInfoTypeForString` which has a clean `-1` sentinel); a static grep is also **cheaper and simpler to maintain** than wrapping every call site. See [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md).
 - **Unused-text-key audit + cleanup:** added [`audit_unused_text_keys.py`](/LLM_Helpers/audit_unused_text_keys.py), which flags mod GameText `<Tag>TXT_KEY_*` entries referenced **nowhere** in the mod, base BTS, or vanilla Civ4 (Python + DLL + XML); dynamically-built (`"TXT_KEY_BUG_OPT_"+id`) and engine-derived (`_PEDIA/_HELP/...`) key families are routed to a separate review bucket to avoid false positives. Used it to **remove confirmed dead GameText entries** from [AdvCiv-SAS_main.xml](/Assets/XML/Text/AdvCiv-SAS_main.xml). See [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5862+) **Handicap XML comparison helper:** added [`compare_handicap_infos.py`](/LLM_Helpers/compare_handicap_infos.py), a report-only, mod-agnostic helper that compares two explicit `CIV4HandicapInfo.xml` file paths, inside or outside this mod folder, by handicap index; shows missing fields as blanks, includes absolute/percentage numeric deltas, and embeds a spreadsheet-friendly TSV matrix. The shipped stable example [`handicap_infos_compared.md`](/LLM_Helpers/examples/handicap_infos_compared.md) compares base AdvCiv 1.12 vs AdvCiv-SAS. See [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md).
 - **Merged** the **old split/interdependent Foreign Advisor** implementation from the two-file setup (`CvForeignAdvisor.py` + `CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py`) into a **single unified** [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) with the **full tab set** (as of now Relations/Glance/Active/Bonus/Info/Tech/Cities). In our findings, **this was the only screen file** using that **interdependent split** pattern, so merging it into one file directly **fixes that inconsistency** and **reduces maintenance burden**; other major screen files such as [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py) and [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py) are lengthy but unified files. By contrast, true alternatives use independent variants (for example BUG/non-BUG [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) / [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) paths), not interdependent split files.
 - **Remove screen-dependent geometry computation** from `__init__` in advisors because this advisor object is created before a reliable screen context exists; doing layout in `interfaceScreen` **ensures correct values for the current resolution**. Keeping **only screen-independent edge constants** in `__init__` ensures **no redundant recomputation** is made again in `interfaceScreen`, and **catches loud screen-dependent errors** in `__init__`.
 - **Heavily refactor and simplify Sevopedia Main** so it is much easier to add, reorder, or modify or otherwise maintain categories. See [Sevopedia reworks (example 0.0)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-00-heavily-refactored-sevopedia-maintain-so-it-is-much-easier-to-maintain-or-customize).

